{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Lean.</b> Thin, as in ״מַדּוּעַ אַתָּה כָּכָה דַל״, ״דְּאַמְנוֹן״ (II Samuel 13)." "<b>And thin of flesh.</b> Every expression of רַקּוֹת in Scripture means lacking flesh — and בְּלַעַז בלוא״ש."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {1 "The la'az בלוא״ש corresponds to Old French blois, 'thin/lean'."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:56.530908221Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}